lokihouse (0.14.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Log queries whose stream set is already known start reading lines
    while the stream lookup runs, instead of after it (about 2 ms less
    per query; plain log filter now level with Loki). New metric
    lokihouse_query_stream_speculations_total.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:32:18 +0100

lokihouse (0.13.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Metric range queries in lokihouse's own engine are split by
    split_queries_by_interval and evaluated in parallel.
  * Log queries filtered in Go read ClickHouse in growing chunks (4x, up
    to 10000 rows), needing fewer round trips. Single-stream log queries
    read in the part's physical order; delete requests come from Loki's
    cache; pinned Loki commit bumped to 39c256e5. Security: strip line
    breaks from client values in the push debug log (CodeQL go/log-
    injection).

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:21:01 +0100

lokihouse (0.12.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Metric queries in lokihouse's own engine (unwrap,
    quantile_over_time) let ClickHouse remove duplicates (FINAL) and
    extract samples on up to GOMAXPROCS cores per query.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:37:56 +0200

lokihouse (0.11.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Schema version 3: run lokihouse -schema.migrate once (all instances
    stopped) after upgrading; it only adds columns and indexes to logs,
    no data copy.
  * Query path: stream-ID sets of any size, time-windowed reads, Tier A
    aggregation pushdown, structured-metadata and parsed label-filter
    pushdown (see CHANGELOG.md).

